      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe a little less confusing with something like\n\n  private class VpnCapsFourplet {\n    NC oldLockdownCaps;\n    NC newLockdownCaps;\n    NC oldVpnCaps;\n    NC newVpnCaps;\n    void setCaps(boolean forLockdown, NC oldCaps, NC newCaps) {\n      if (forLockdown) {\n        oldLockdownCaps \u003d oldCaps;\n        newLockdownCaps \u003d newCaps;\n      } else {\n        oldVpnCaps \u003d oldCaps;\n        newVpnCaps \u003d newCaps;\n      }\n    }\n\n  private void handleLockdownOrVpnChanged() {\n    final boolean naiIsForlockdown \u003d nai.networkMisc.forLockdown;\n    final VpnCapsFourplet caps \u003d new VpnCapsFourplet();\n    caps.setCaps(naiIsForLockdown, prevNc, newNc);\n    for (...) {\n      final NC otherAgentCaps \u003d getVpnCapabilitiesIfApplyToUid(nri.mUid, !naiIsforLockdown);\n      caps.setCaps(!naiIsForLockdown, otherAgentCaps, otherAgentCaps);\n      maybeNotifyBlockedForNetworkRequest(nai, nri, curMetered, curMetered,\n              mRestrictBackground, mRestrictBackground,\n              caps.oldLockdownCaps, caps.newLockdownCaps,\n              caps.oldVpnCaps, caps.newVpnCaps);\n    }\n  }\n\n\nAnother option would be :\n\n  private void handleLockdownOrVpnChanged() {\n    final Pair\u003cNC, NC\u003e lockdownCaps \u003d new Pair\u003c\u003e();\n    final Pair\u003cNC, NC\u003e vpnCaps \u003d new Pair\u003c\u003e();\n    final Pair\u003cNC, NC\u003e missingCaps;\n    if (nai.networkMisc.forLockdown) {\n      lockdownCaps.first \u003d oldNc;\n      lockdownCaps.second \u003d newNc;\n      missingCaps \u003d vpnCaps;\n    } else {\n      vpnCaps.first \u003d oldNc;\n      vpnCaps.second \u003d newNc;\n      missingCaps \u003d lockdownCaps;\n    }\n    for (...) {\n      final NC otherAgentCaps \u003d getVpnCapabilitiesIfApplyToUid(nri.mUid, !nai.forLockdown);\n      missingCaps.first \u003d otherAgentCaps;\n      missingCaps.second \u003d otherAgentCaps;\n      maybeNotifyBlockedForNetworkRequest(nai, nri, curMetered, curMetered,\n              mRestrictBackground, mRestrictBackground,\n              lockdownCaps.first, lockdownCaps.seconfd,\n              vpnCaps.first, vpnCaps.second);\n    }\n  }\n\n\n\nWDYT ?\n\n(I\u0027m happy with your current code BTW, it\u0027s just a suggestion)",
